Download for Windows ARM PC? Windows on ARM. The app isn't code-signed yet, so Windows may warn you: choose More info → Run anyway.
Your system
Linux
A tray app on a desktop, or a command line and a service on a server or a Pi.
@a.download
@a.href=https://github.com/alonsovidales/otc/releases/download/desktop/otc-sync-linux-amd64
@a.download
@a.href=https://github.com/alonsovidales/otc/releases/download/desktop/otc-sync-linux-arm64
Download for Linux ARM (e.g. a Raspberry Pi)? Linux ARM64. Then:install -Dm755 otc-sync-linux-* ~/.local/bin/otc-sync && otc-sync
Your system
macOS
A menu bar app with the same folders and sync rules, on the Mac App Store, which keeps it up to date for you.
@a.href=https://apps.apple.com/app/id6814658734
Get it on the Mac App Store
@a.href=https://github.com/alonsovidales/otc
@a.href=https://github.com/alonsovidales/otc/releases/tag/desktop
Every update is signed. The apps only install a new version after checking its signature against the project's release key, the same key that signs the device updates. The source is on GitHub, and every file is listed on the desktop release.
Phone apps
Your photos, backed up from your phone
Back up your photos and videos as you take them, browse everything on your device, share with friends, and set up a new device over Bluetooth.
Your system
iPhone and iPad
Backs up your photo library, iCloud photos included, and shows your device's photos, files and friends' posts.
Coming soon to the App Store
Your system
Android
The same app for Android phones and tablets: photo backup, your device's files and photos, and friends' posts.
@a.href=https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=cloud.offthe.otc
Get it on Google Play
What it is
One device, four ways to reach it
A Raspberry Pi in your home stores everything; native apps on every platform keep it in sync and let you browse, search, and share it.
💾
The device
A Raspberry Pi 5 with a card for the system and two storage cards mirrored in RAID-1, storing your originals unprocessed and uncompressed — encrypted at rest, with a key that only your password unlocks.
🖥️
Desktop client
macOS, Windows and Linux apps that keep chosen folders on your computer in two-way sync with the device, automatically.
📱
Mobile app
iOS and Android apps that back up your camera roll in the background, in full resolution, and double as the social feed.
🌐
Web app
Everything above, from any browser — sign in with just your password, no app install required.
🔍
AI search, kept private
Every photo is auto-tagged locally on the device, so you can search "beach" or "dog" instantly — nothing is sent to a third party to do it.
🚫
No toxic feed
The social side has no ads, no influencers, no engagement algorithm — just posts from people you've actually approved as friends.
👨‍👩‍👧
One device, the whole family
Give everyone at home their own account on the same device — their own photo backup, library and password, each encrypted with its own key. You manage the accounts, but you can't open the photos and files in them.
🔗
Share collections with a link
Send a collection of photos to anyone as a link that expires. They open it in their browser, with no account or app, and can download the originals.
⚡
Fast at home
At home the apps talk straight to the device over your own network, so a whole holiday's photos back up at Wi-Fi speed instead of crawling over the internet.
